-# Prepared-context owner-identity repair
+# Prepared-context packet owner-identity repair
 
 ## Outcome
 
-PASS for this bounded repair unit.
+PASS.
 
 ## Defect
 
-The public `build_prepared_context_packet` wrapper did not expose the caller-owned producer identity and `derivedfrom` lineage required by the accepted M04 DMPV3 boundary. Its physical Tier A callers therefore failed before packet construction with:
-
-- `module_version must be a caller-owned governed identity`; or
-- `scenarioid must be a caller-owned governed identity`.
-
-The wrapper also supplied source artefacts, input fingerprints and degraded limitations without the matching owner validators and degraded-consumer restriction required by the strict packet builder.
+The public `nvda_desk.preparation.context_packet.build_prepared_context_packet` helper did not expose or forward the caller-owned producer identity required by current M04/K07 law. Calls through the lower-level M04 builder correctly rejected the resulting packet for absent `module_version`, `module_instance_id`, or execution context. The same helper also failed to activate conditional K07 lineage fields when the caller explicitly supplied parent, dependency, or review lineage.
 
 ## Repair
 
-`src/nvda_desk/preparation/context_packet.py` now:
-
-- accepts caller-owned `module_version`, `module_instance_id` and `derivedfrom` values;
-- forwards those values unchanged to the canonical M04 builder;
-- binds source-artifact and input-fingerprint checks to the prepared payload;
-- declares only the admitted prepared-context owner-check names;
-- validates degraded limitations against actual failed enrichments; and
-- marks degraded prepared context as unable to create positive permission.
-
-No identity is generated or defaulted by the wrapper. Missing producer identity remains a hard failure.
-
-## Proof
-
-Focused M03/M04/M09 boundary proof:
-
-```text
-99 passed in 1.24s
-```
+- Added caller-supplied `module_version`, `module_instance_id`, and `derivedfrom` parameters.
+- Forwarded those identities without synthesising defaults.
+- Bound source-artifact and input-fingerprint validators to the actual prepared snapshot lineage.
+- Bound the exact prepared-context K07 owner-check set.
+- Activated conditional parent, dependency, and review lineage only when explicitly supplied.
+- Preserved degraded validation and added a fail-closed consumer restriction when preparation enrichments fail.
+- Added proof that missing producer identity remains rejected.
 
-Complete physical `upstream_cognition` partition:
+## Validation
 
 ```text
-71 passed in 0.73s
+71 passed in 0.70s
 ```
 
-The complete physical Tier A partition census is now:
+Complete physical upstream-cognition directory.
 
 ```text
-1,842 passed
-46 failed
-0 errors
-42 partitions
+106 passed in 0.73s
 ```
 
-All 46 remaining failures belong to the separately adjudicated FWD004 row-level packet-carriage gap. No prepared-context failure remains.
+Upstream cognition plus current M03 K05/K06 and reference-packet carriage proof.
 
 ## Ruled out
 
-- synthesising module, run, trace or scenario identities;
-- weakening M04 owner checks;
-- accepting a degraded prepared packet without an explicit consumer restriction;
-- changing prepared payload semantics;
-- treating the unresolved FWD004 failures as part of this repair.
+- generated module versions or module-instance identities;
+- generated scenario identity;
+- weakening M04/K07 owner checks;
+- treating degraded prepared context as positive permission;
+- changing M03 preparation semantics.
